      {
        "id": 37819,
        "name": "dypaca",
        "username": "dypaca",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dypaca/{size}/2079_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-12-11T02:10:14.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Koga\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/koga/48/2058_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Koga:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>Reckless wrote:</b><br><blockquote>Does that mean they're not destroyed?&nbsp; So if there are cards beside Self-Destruct Sequence and it is destroyed, does Haka not get to draw more cards from Dominion for the cards next to it because they're just moved to the trash rather than destroyed?&nbsp;\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nSelf-Destruct Sequence is different, on the card it says the pile is destroyed along with the card.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>It says the pile and this card are destroyed if the countdown pile is full.&nbsp; It does not say that the countdown pile is destroyed if this card is destroyed by some other means.&nbsp; I would say it should work the same as omnicannon.</p>",
